=== WaveVM Mode B Multi-VM Isolation Test ===

Test 1: Configure three nodes with different capability profiles
  ✓ Node 17: KVM + Mode B (executor)
  ✓ Node 18: TCG + Mode B (executor)
  ✓ Node 19: Mode B only (memory-only)

Test 2: Verify capability constraints
  Node 17 capabilities: KVM execution + Mode B memory
    - Can execute VM with KVM backend
    - Can serve Mode B page protocol
  Node 18 capabilities: TCG execution + Mode B memory
    - Can execute VM with TCG backend
    - Can serve Mode B page protocol
  Node 19 capabilities: Mode B memory only
    - CANNOT execute VM (no vCPU slots)
    - CAN serve Mode B page protocol
    - Suitable for memory-only participant role

Test 3: Mode B isolation properties
  Each VM has isolated:
    - GPA namespace (guest physical address space)
    - Page version tracking per-VM
    - Directory node assignment per-page
    - Commit operation identity (vm_id + operation_id)
  Mode B protocol ensures:
    - READ returns page + version + directory identity
    - COMMIT requires base_version match
    - ACK carries directory authority

Test 4: Multi-VM deployment scenarios
  Scenario A: Two VMs on different executor nodes
    - VM 256 on node 17 (KVM)
    - VM 257 on node 18 (TCG)
    - Both use node 19 for remote memory
    - Isolated by (vm_id, gpa) tuple
  Scenario B: Co-located VMs with shared memory node
    - VM 256 and VM 257 on node 17 (KVM)
    - Both use node 19 for memory
    - Kernel context isolation per VM
    - Runtime name namespace isolation per VM

Test 5: Verify cluster has heterogeneous capability mix
  Cluster record set:
    - 3 nodes (2 executor + 1 memory-only)
    - 5 capability records total
    - 2 execution capabilities (KVM, TCG)
    - 3 Mode B memory capabilities
  ✓ Cluster supports both execution modes
  ✓ Cluster includes memory-only participant

=== Mode B multi-VM capability and digest computation PASS ===
NOTE: This test verifies capability structure construction and digest calculation.
      It does not run actual VMs or validate GPA/version/directory runtime behavior.
mode-b-multivm: PASS
